# This file exists for the BUILD, not for git — the repository root's .gitignore
# already covers every pattern below.
#
# Hatchling excludes VCS-ignored files by default, and it finds the ignore file
# by walking UP from its own root (runtime/python), then matches the patterns it
# finds relative to THAT root. So the repository's `/leoflow` line — anchored to
# the repo root, where it names the built Go binary, and which git correctly does
# not apply here — read to hatchling as "the leoflow directory at my root" and
# silently dropped runtime/python/leoflow from the wheel. The build succeeded and
# the wheel simply had no authoring package in it (#17).
#
# hatchling's locate_file stops at the FIRST .gitignore going up, so this one
# shadows the repository's entirely: the root cause is gone rather than opted out
# of, VCS exclusion keeps protecting both the wheel and the sdist, and a
# developer's global ~/.gitignore can no longer reach a build run from
# ~/.leoflow/pysrc. Opting out with `ignore-vcs = true` did the opposite — the
# package came back and so did every dirty file in these directories: measured,
# the sdist then shipped .coverage from the maintainer's own tree.
#
# Mirrors the repository root's patterns that can apply inside these two package
# directories. Anything the root ignores and this file does not will ride into
# the wheel, so keep them in step.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
*.egg
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
.venv/
venv/
dist/
.env
*.log
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
